---
import MissionLayout from '../../layouts/MissionLayout.astro';
---

<MissionLayout
  slug="mbfs-sea"
  heading="Mercedes-Benz Financial Services - SEA region"
  timeline="—"
  status="Shipped / MVP"
  heroImage="/assets/projects/mb-thumbnail.avif"
  explorerGradient="linear-gradient(40deg, #141414 0%, #242424 100%)"
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">1. The TL;DR <span class="case-section-sub">(Executive Summary)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Purpose</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Revamp the customer portal to deliver a better digital experience and make it more useful throughout the financial contract journey.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Problem</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The portal relied on APIs and a database managed by a third-party vendor. This limited how much the team could change independently and meant the experience had to be designed around the existing backend’s capabilities, with ongoing coordination to keep the interface and system aligned.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Solution</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">We refreshed the portal UI and expanded its utility within the constraints of the existing platform, working closely with the backend team to align the experience with available APIs and system capabilities.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Impact</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Customers gained more self-service options in the portal, including managing payments and renewing financial contracts, alongside a connection to the Mercedes-Benz app for mileage control.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">2. Strategy &amp; Discovery</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Insight</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A customer portal could do more than provide account information: it could help customers take care of key tasks across their financial contract journey. Making that useful required shaping the experience around the capabilities of the existing platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Stakeholders</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The work called for close collaboration between design, product, and technical teams, as well as coordination with the third-party vendor responsible for the APIs and database. Regular alignment helped connect the intended customer experience with what the backend could support.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Constraint</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The backend APIs and database were controlled by a third-party vendor, so the team could not change the underlying system independently. The interface and feature scope had to account for those dependencies and stay aligned with available backend functionality.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">3. Execution <span class="case-section-sub">(The &ldquo;How&rdquo;)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Key Decision</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">We focused on improving the customer-facing experience and making better use of the existing platform, rather than treating a backend replacement as a prerequisite. This allowed the team to move the portal forward while coordinating each experience with the systems and APIs available.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Design Leadership</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">I helped guide the experience from research and design through development readiness, working with product owners and technical teams to translate customer and business needs into a practical portal UI. Design decisions balanced a clearer customer journey with the constraints of the existing backend.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Highlights</h3>
      <!-- Gallery -->
      <div class="gallery-wrap">
        <div class="gallery-track-wrap">
          <div class="gallery-track" id="galleryTrack">
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/mb-thumbnail.avif" alt="Project screen 1" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/mb-thumbnail.avif" alt="Project screen 2" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-controls">
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryPrev" aria-label="Previous">&#8592; Back</button>
          <span class="gallery-counter" id="galleryCounter">1 / 2</span>
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryNext" aria-label="Next">Next &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
  
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">4. Outcome &amp; Lessons</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">KPIs</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">No quantified outcome metrics are available to share. The delivered outcome was a portal with expanded self-service capabilities, including payment management, financial contract renewal, and a connection with the Mercedes-Benz app for mileage control.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Post-Launch</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The shipped MVP gave customers more ways to manage their financial services online. The project also underscored how closely the quality of a digital experience depends on ongoing coordination between interface design and the backend systems that support it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Next Steps</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A next phase could use customer feedback and usage data to identify friction in payment, renewal, and mileage-related tasks, then prioritize improvements with the product and backend teams. This would help guide both portal refinements and any API or platform changes needed to support them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MissionLayout>
